"""
AI Trading Engine v13
Research-grade long-only ML backtester.

Design goals:
- No same-bar lookahead: signal at close t -> entry at next available open.
- Purged walk-forward validation with an explicit purge window AND
  label-exit-based purging (belt-and-suspenders), plus embargo.
- Regime-dependent feature selection & modeling: a market regime
  (trend x volatility bucket, derived from the benchmark) is computed
  and used to train regime-conditional model bundles in addition to
  the combined (regime-agnostic) bundle. Predictions blend both.
- Robust per-asset panel handling (no cross-asset label shifts).
- Triple-barrier-inspired labels using future path, not only terminal close.
- Probability calibration from a validation split inside each training fold.
- Cross-sectional ranking of OOS opportunities.
- Portfolio/risk controls, ATR exits, costs and slippage.
- Monte Carlo robustness test: block-bootstrap on realized trade returns
  and on the daily equity curve to quantify how much of the result could
  plausibly be sequencing luck vs. a repeatable edge.
- Full daily equity curve and diagnostics.

v13 changes vs v12:
- FIX: `purge_days` was defined in Config and exposed in the UI but never
  actually applied anywhere in walk_forward(). It now removes any training
  row within `purge_days` calendar days of the OOS test start, on top of
  the existing label-exit-based purge.
- NEW: regime detection (compute_regime) + regime-conditional model bundles
  (train_models / predict_models) with a blend weight.
- NEW: monte_carlo_robustness() — block bootstrap over trade returns and
  over the daily equity curve.
- NEW: Sortino, Calmar, CVaR(5%), exposure and turnover in performance_metrics.
"""

